Now I understand the architecture. The `coach-claude` package provides:
1. A `run` command that can run the server with either SSE or stdio transport
2. SSE mode: `coach-claude run --transport sse --port 8787` - runs an SSE server on localhost:8787
3. Stdio mode: `coach-claude run --transport stdio` (default) - runs MCP over stdio

